module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.EffectiveCartierCriterion
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.IdealSheafSections.DualBasisOne
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Divisors.IdealSheafSections.KernelSections
import StacksCore.Tactic.EgaSgaAttribute

/-!
# The sections of the ideal sheaf of a closed subscheme

A closed subscheme of a scheme `X` is recorded by an `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData`,
which carries an ideal `I.ideal U ⊆ Γ(X, U)` for every *affine* open `U` and the closed immersion
`I.subschemeι` it cuts out. Its ideal *sheaf* is a sheaf of `𝒪_X`-modules, namely the categorical
kernel `Stacks.ClosedImmersion.idealSheaf` of `𝒪_X ⟶ i_* 𝒪_D`. Nothing connects the two: the
ideals live only on affine opens, and the kernel is a limit in a category of sheaves of modules.

This file provides the bridge. Over an arbitrary open `V`, a section of the ideal sheaf is exactly
a section of `𝒪_X` over `V` annihilated by `I.subschemeι`
(`Stacks.Divisors.subschemeι_app_eq_zero_iff_exists_idealSheafSection`), and over an *affine* open
it is exactly an element of `I.ideal V`
(`Stacks.Divisors.mem_ideal_iff_exists_idealSheafSection`).

The bridge is then used to prove the forward direction of Stacks Tag 01WS. If the ideal on an
affine open `U` is generated by a single nonzerodivisor `f`, then over *every* open `W ⊆ U` the
sections of the ideal sheaf are the multiples of `f|_W`, and `f|_W` is again a nonzerodivisor; so
multiplication by the section of the ideal sheaf determined by `f` is bijective over the whole
slice site `Opens X / U`, which is precisely the rank-one dual basis that
`Stacks.Divisors.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_forall_exists_dualBasisOne` consumes. Hence a closed
subscheme which is cut out, near every point of its support, by a nonzerodivisor on an affine open
is an effective Cartier divisor.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Divisors.subschemeStructureHom`: the map `𝒪_X ⟶ i_* 𝒪_D` of the closed immersion
  cutting out `I`, as a morphism of sheaves of `𝒪_X`-modules; the ideal sheaf is its kernel.
* `Stacks.Divisors.idealSheafSection`: a section of the ideal sheaf over an open, read as a
  section of the structure sheaf.
* `Stacks.Divisors.dualBasisOneOfPrincipal`: on an affine open where the ideal is generated by a
  nonzerodivisor, the rank-one dual basis of the ideal sheaf.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Divisors.subschemeι_app_eq_zero_iff_exists_idealSheafSection` and
  `Stacks.Divisors.mem_ideal_iff_exists_idealSheafSection`: the bridge, over an arbitrary open and
  over an affine open.
* `Stacks.Divisors.mem_nonZeroDivisors_res`: a nonzerodivisor on an affine open restricts to a
  nonzerodivisor on every open subset of it.
* `Stacks.Divisors.exists_mul_of_subschemeι_app_eq_zero`: over every open subset of an affine open
  on which the ideal is generated by a nonzerodivisor `f`, a section annihilated by the closed
  immersion is a multiple of `f`.
* `Stacks.Divisors.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_forall_mem_support`: the direction (2) ⇒ (1) of
  Stacks Tag 01WS.
* `Stacks.Divisors.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_top`: the empty closed subscheme is an effective
  Cartier divisor.

## Implementation notes

**Extending from affine opens to arbitrary opens.** Both halves of the local computation — that
`f|_W` is a nonzerodivisor and that every annihilated section is a multiple of it — are local on
`W`, and are proved by descending to the basic opens of the ambient affine open `U`, which form a
basis of `U`. Basic opens are used rather than arbitrary affine opens because the nonzerodivisor
half needs the restriction `Γ(X, U) → Γ(X, W)` to be flat, which for a basic open is
`IsAffineOpen.isLocalization_basicOpen` together with
`IsLocalization.nonZeroDivisors_le_comap`, whereas for a general affine open `W ⊆ U` it is not
available in this form. On a basic open the ideal is computed by
`Scheme.IdealSheafData.map_ideal` and `Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_subschemeι_app`.

**Points off the support.** Stacks 01WS (2) only constrains the points of `D`, while the
dual-basis criterion needs a cover of all of `X`. Off the support the ideal sheaf is the whole
structure sheaf: `Stacks.Divisors.exists_affineOpens_ideal_eq_top` produces an affine open on
which the ideal is the unit ideal, generated by the nonzerodivisor `1`, so the same construction
applies there with `f = 1`.

**Spellings.** The sections of the structure sheaf appear in two forms, `Γ(X, V)` and
`(structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace).obj.obj (op V)`, which have the same
carrier and the same ring structure but are not syntactically equal, so instance resolution does
not connect them: `c • y` for `c : Γ(X, V)` and `y` a section of a sheaf of modules does not
elaborate. `Stacks.Divisors.idealSheafSection` therefore lands in `Γ(X, V)`, and the only
statement mixing the two, `Stacks.Divisors.idealSheafSection_smulSectionMap`, writes the scalar
action as `Stacks.SheafOfModules.smulSectionMap`, which fixes the module-side spelling.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01WR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01WR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01C2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01C2)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace Opposite
open RingedSpaceModuleAdjunction

universe u

namespace Stacks.Divisors

variable {X : Scheme.{u}}

/-! ### Restriction and gluing of sections of the structure sheaf -/

/-- Restricting a section of the structure sheaf twice is restricting it once. -/
lemma res_res {U V W : X.Opens} (h₁ : W ≤ V) (h₂ : V ≤ U) (f : Γ(X, U)) :
    X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h₁).op (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h₂).op f) =
      X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (h₁.trans h₂)).op f := by
  rw [← ConcreteCategory.comp_apply, ← Functor.map_comp]
  rfl

/-- Two sections of the structure sheaf agreeing on a cover are equal. This is
`TopCat.Sheaf.eq_of_locally_eq'` in the `Γ(X, -)` spelling. -/
lemma eq_of_locally_eq {ι : Type*} (V : ι → X.Opens) (W : X.Opens) (iVW : ∀ i, V i ⟶ W)
    (hcover : W ≤ iSup V) (s t : Γ(X, W))
    (h : ∀ i, X.presheaf.map (iVW i).op s = X.presheaf.map (iVW i).op t) : s = t :=
  TopCat.Sheaf.eq_of_locally_eq' X.sheaf V W iVW hcover s t h

/-- A compatible family of sections of the structure sheaf on a cover glues uniquely. This is
`TopCat.Sheaf.existsUnique_gluing'` in the `Γ(X, -)` spelling. -/
lemma existsUnique_gluing {ι : Type*} (V : ι → X.Opens) (W : X.Opens) (iVW : ∀ i, V i ⟶ W)
    (hcover : W ≤ iSup V) (sf : ∀ i, Γ(X, V i))
    (h : TopCat.Presheaf.IsCompatible X.presheaf V sf) :
    ∃! s : Γ(X, W), ∀ i, X.presheaf.map (iVW i).op s = sf i :=
  TopCat.Sheaf.existsUnique_gluing' X.sheaf V W iVW hcover sf h

/-! ### Nonzerodivisors restrict to nonzerodivisors -/

/-- A nonzerodivisor on an affine open restricts to a nonzerodivisor on a basic open: the
restriction is a localization, hence flat. -/
lemma mem_nonZeroDivisors_res_basicOpen {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {f : Γ(X, U)}
    (hf : f ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, U)) (g : Γ(X, U)) :
    X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (X.basicOpen_le g)).op f ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, X.basicOpen g) := by
  have := hU.isLocalization_basicOpen g
  exact IsLocalization.nonZeroDivisors_le_comap
    (M := Submonoid.powers g) (S := Γ(X, X.basicOpen g)) hf

/-- An open subset `W` of an affine open `U` is covered by basic opens of `U` contained in `W`. -/
private lemma exists_basicOpen_cover {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {W : X.Opens}
    (hWU : W ≤ U) :
    ∃ g : W → Γ(X, U), (∀ x, X.basicOpen (g x) ≤ W) ∧ W ≤ iSup fun x => X.basicOpen (g x) := by
  choose g hg hgmem using fun x : W => hU.exists_basicOpen_le (V := W) x (hWU x.2)
  exact ⟨g, hg, fun y hy => Opens.mem_iSup.2 ⟨⟨y, hy⟩, hgmem ⟨y, hy⟩⟩⟩

/-- **A nonzerodivisor on an affine open restricts to a nonzerodivisor on every open subset.**
Being killed by the restricted section is a local condition, and the basic opens of `U` contained
in `W` cover `W`. -/
lemma mem_nonZeroDivisors_res {U : X.Opens} (hU : IsAffineOpen U) {f : Γ(X, U)}
    (hf : f ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, U)) {W : X.Opens} (hWU : W ≤ U) :
    X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWU).op f ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, W) := by
  have key : ∀ r : Γ(X, W), r * X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWU).op f = 0 → r = 0 := by
    intro r hr
    obtain ⟨g, hg, hcover⟩ := exists_basicOpen_cover hU hWU
    refine eq_of_locally_eq (fun x : W => X.basicOpen (g x)) W (fun x => homOfLE (hg x))
      hcover r 0 fun x => ?_
    rw [map_zero]
    refine (mul_right_mem_nonZeroDivisors_eq_zero_iff
      (mem_nonZeroDivisors_res_basicOpen hU hf (g x))).1 ?_
    rw [← res_res (hg x) hWU f, ← map_mul, hr, map_zero]
  exact mem_nonZeroDivisors_iff.2 ⟨fun r hr => key r (by rw [mul_comm]; exact hr), key⟩

/-! ### The ideal cut out on an open subset of an affine open -/

/-- Restricting a section annihilated by the closed immersion keeps it annihilated. -/
lemma subschemeι_app_eq_zero_of_le (I : X.IdealSheafData) {W W' : X.Opens} (h : W' ≤ W)
    {r : Γ(X, W)} (hr : I.subschemeι.app W r = 0) :
    I.subschemeι.app W' (X.presheaf.map (homOfLE h).op r) = 0 := by
  have hnat := ConcreteCategory.congr_hom (I.subschemeι.naturality (homOfLE h).op) r
  rw [CommRingCat.comp_apply, CommRingCat.comp_apply, hr, map_zero] at hnat
  exact hnat

/-- On an affine open `V` contained in an affine open `U` on which the ideal is generated by `f`,
a section annihilated by the closed immersion is a multiple of `f|_V`. This is
`Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_subschemeι_app` combined with `Scheme.IdealSheafData.map_ideal`. -/
lemma exists_mul_of_subschemeι_app_eq_zero_affine (I : X.IdealSheafData) {U V : X.affineOpens}
    (hVU : V ≤ U) {f : Γ(X, (U : X.Opens))} (hf : I.ideal U = Ideal.span {f})
    (r : Γ(X, (V : X.Opens))) (hr : I.subschemeι.app (V : X.Opens) r = 0) :
    ∃ c : Γ(X, (V : X.Opens)), r = c * X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hVU).op f := by
  have h : r ∈ I.ideal V := by
    rw [← I.ker_subschemeι_app V]
    exact hr
  rw [← I.map_ideal hVU, hf, Ideal.map_span, Set.image_singleton,
    Ideal.mem_span_singleton'] at h
  obtain ⟨c, hc⟩ := h
  exact ⟨c, hc.symm⟩

/-- **Over an arbitrary open subset of an affine open on which the ideal is generated by a
nonzerodivisor `f`, every annihilated section is a multiple of `f`.** The quotients produced on
the basic opens covering `W` agree on overlaps because `f` restricts to a nonzerodivisor there,
so they glue. -/
lemma exists_mul_of_subschemeι_app_eq_zero (I : X.IdealSheafData) (U : X.affineOpens)
    {f : Γ(X, (U : X.Opens))} (hf : I.ideal U = Ideal.span {f})
    (hfnzd : f ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, (U : X.Opens)))
    {W : X.Opens} (hWU : W ≤ (U : X.Opens)) (r : Γ(X, W))
    (hr : I.subschemeι.app W r = 0) :
    ∃ c : Γ(X, W), r = c * X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWU).op f := by
  obtain ⟨g, hg, hcover⟩ := exists_basicOpen_cover U.2 hWU
  set V : W → X.Opens := fun x => X.basicOpen (g x)
  have hVU : ∀ x, V x ≤ (U : X.Opens) := fun x => (hg x).trans hWU
  have hdiv : ∀ x : W, ∃ c : Γ(X, V x),
      X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hg x)).op r = c * X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (hVU x)).op f :=
    fun x => exists_mul_of_subschemeι_app_eq_zero_affine I (V := X.affineBasicOpen (g x))
      (X.affineBasicOpen_le (g x)) hf _ (subschemeι_app_eq_zero_of_le I (hg x) hr)
  choose c hc using hdiv
  have key : ∀ (x : W) (A : X.Opens) (i : A ⟶ V x),
      X.presheaf.map i.op (c x) * X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (i.le.trans (hVU x))).op f =
        X.presheaf.map (homOfLE (i.le.trans (hg x))).op r := by
    intro x A i
    have h : X.presheaf.map i.op = X.presheaf.map (homOfLE i.le).op := rfl
    rw [h, ← res_res i.le (hg x) r, hc x, map_mul, res_res]
  have hcompat : TopCat.Presheaf.IsCompatible X.presheaf V c := by
    intro x y
    rw [← sub_eq_zero]
    refine (mul_right_mem_nonZeroDivisors_eq_zero_iff
      (mem_nonZeroDivisors_res U.2 hfnzd
        ((Opens.infLELeft (V x) (V y)).le.trans (hVU x)))).1 ?_
    rw [sub_mul, key x _ (Opens.infLELeft (V x) (V y)),
      key y _ (Opens.infLERight (V x) (V y))]
    exact sub_eq_zero.2 rfl
  obtain ⟨cc, hcc, -⟩ := existsUnique_gluing V W (fun x => homOfLE (hg x)) hcover c hcompat
  refine ⟨cc, eq_of_locally_eq V W (fun x => homOfLE (hg x)) hcover _ _ fun x => ?_⟩
  rw [map_mul, res_res, hcc x]
  exact hc x

/-! ### Sections of the ideal sheaf -/

/-- The map `𝒪_X ⟶ i_* 𝒪_D` of the closed immersion cutting out the closed subscheme `I`, as a
morphism of sheaves of `𝒪_X`-modules. The ideal sheaf `Stacks.Divisors.idealSheafOfModules` is
its kernel, by definition. -/
abbrev subschemeStructureHom (I : X.IdealSheafData) :
    SheafOfModules.unit (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace) ⟶
      (SheafOfModules.pushforward
        (structureSheafHom I.subschemeι.toLRSHom.toShHom)).obj
        (SheafOfModules.unit (structureSheafRing I.subscheme.toRingedSpace)) :=
  SheafOfModules.unitToPushforwardObjUnit (structureSheafHom I.subschemeι.toLRSHom.toShHom)

/-- On sections over an open set, the structure-sheaf map of the closed immersion is the map
`I.subschemeι.app` of the morphism of schemes. -/
lemma subschemeStructureHom_val_app_apply (I : X.IdealSheafData) {V : X.Opens} (r : Γ(X, V)) :
    (subschemeStructureHom I).val.app (op V) r = I.subschemeι.app V r := rfl

/-- **A section of the ideal sheaf, read as a section of the structure sheaf.** This is the
inclusion `ℐ_D ⟶ 𝒪_X` on sections over an open set. -/
def idealSheafSection (I : X.IdealSheafData) {V : X.Opens}
    (y : (idealSheafOfModules I).val.obj (op V)) : Γ(X, V) :=
  (kernel.ι (subschemeStructureHom I)).val.app (op V) y

/-- The inclusion of the ideal sheaf is injective on sections. -/
lemma idealSheafSection_injective (I : X.IdealSheafData) {V : X.Opens} :
    Function.Injective (idealSheafSection I (V := V)) :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.injective_kernel_ι_app (subschemeStructureHom I) (op V)

/-- A section of the ideal sheaf is annihilated by the closed immersion. -/
lemma subschemeι_app_idealSheafSection (I : X.IdealSheafData) {V : X.Opens}
    (y : (idealSheafOfModules I).val.obj (op V)) :
    I.subschemeι.app V (idealSheafSection I y) = 0 :=
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.app_kernel_ι_app (subschemeStructureHom I) (op V) y

/-- **The bridge, over an arbitrary open.** A section of the structure sheaf over `V` comes from
the ideal sheaf exactly when the closed immersion annihilates it. -/
theorem subschemeι_app_eq_zero_iff_exists_idealSheafSection (I : X.IdealSheafData) {V : X.Opens}
    (r : Γ(X, V)) :
    I.subschemeι.app V r = 0 ↔ ∃ y, idealSheafSection I y = r := by
  refine ⟨fun h => Stacks.SheafOfModules.exists_kernel_section
    (subschemeStructureHom I) (op V) r h, ?_⟩
  rintro ⟨y, rfl⟩
  exact subschemeι_app_idealSheafSection I y

/-- **The bridge, over an affine open.** The sections of the ideal sheaf over an affine open `V`
are exactly the elements of the ideal `I.ideal V` that the closed subscheme cuts out there. -/
theorem mem_ideal_iff_exists_idealSheafSection (I : X.IdealSheafData) (V : X.affineOpens)
    (r : Γ(X, (V : X.Opens))) :
    r ∈ I.ideal V ↔ ∃ y, idealSheafSection I y = r := by
  rw [← I.ker_subschemeι_app V]
  exact subschemeι_app_eq_zero_iff_exists_idealSheafSection I r

/-- The inclusion of the ideal sheaf is `𝒪_X`-linear. The scalar action is written with
`Stacks.SheafOfModules.smulSectionMap` because the two spellings of the sections of the structure
sheaf do not share instances; see the implementation notes. -/
lemma idealSheafSection_smulSectionMap (I : X.IdealSheafData) {V : X.Opens}
    (y : (idealSheafOfModules I).val.obj (op V)) (c : Γ(X, V)) :
    idealSheafSection I (Stacks.SheafOfModules.smulSectionMap
        (𝒪 := X.sheaf.obj) (h𝒪 := (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace).property) y c) =
      c * idealSheafSection I y :=
  ((kernel.ι (subschemeStructureHom I)).val.app (op V)).hom.map_smul c y

/-- The inclusion of the ideal sheaf commutes with the restriction maps. -/
lemma idealSheafSection_resSection (I : X.IdealSheafData) {U : X.Opens} (V : (Over U)ᵒᵖ)
    (y : (idealSheafOfModules I).val.obj (op U)) :
    idealSheafSection I (Stacks.SheafOfModules.resSection
        (𝒪 := X.sheaf.obj) (h𝒪 := (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace).property) V y) =
      X.presheaf.map V.unop.hom.op (idealSheafSection I y) :=
  PresheafOfModules.naturality_apply (kernel.ι (subschemeStructureHom I)).val V.unop.hom.op y

/-! ### The rank-one dual basis of a principal ideal sheaf -/

/-- **Multiplication by a generating nonzerodivisor is bijective on the sections of the ideal
sheaf over every open subset of the affine open.** Injectivity is the nonzerodivisor property of
the restricted generator, surjectivity is the division statement
`Stacks.Divisors.exists_mul_of_subschemeι_app_eq_zero`. -/
theorem bijective_smulSectionMap_resSection (I : X.IdealSheafData) (U : X.affineOpens)
    {f : Γ(X, (U : X.Opens))} (hf : I.ideal U = Ideal.span {f})
    (hfnzd : f ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, (U : X.Opens)))
    {e : (idealSheafOfModules I).val.obj (op (U : X.Opens))} (he : idealSheafSection I e = f)
    (V : (Over (U : X.Opens))ᵒᵖ) :
    Function.Bijective (Stacks.SheafOfModules.smulSectionMap
      (𝒪 := X.sheaf.obj) (h𝒪 := (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace).property)
      (Stacks.SheafOfModules.resSection V e)) := by
  have hWU : V.unop.left ≤ (U : X.Opens) := V.unop.hom.le
  have hres : idealSheafSection I (Stacks.SheafOfModules.resSection
      (𝒪 := X.sheaf.obj) (h𝒪 := (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace).property) V e) =
      X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWU).op f := by
    rw [idealSheafSection_resSection, he]
    rfl
  have hmul : ∀ d : Γ(X, V.unop.left),
      idealSheafSection I (Stacks.SheafOfModules.smulSectionMap
          (𝒪 := X.sheaf.obj) (h𝒪 := (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace).property)
          (Stacks.SheafOfModules.resSection V e) d) =
        d * X.presheaf.map (homOfLE hWU).op f := by
    intro d
    rw [idealSheafSection_smulSectionMap, hres]
  refine ⟨fun c c' hcc => ?_, fun y => ?_⟩
  · refine (mul_cancel_right_mem_nonZeroDivisors
      (mem_nonZeroDivisors_res U.2 hfnzd hWU)).1 ?_
    rw [← hmul c, ← hmul c', hcc]
  · obtain ⟨c, hcy⟩ := exists_mul_of_subschemeι_app_eq_zero I U hf hfnzd hWU
      (idealSheafSection I y) (subschemeι_app_idealSheafSection I y)
    exact ⟨c, idealSheafSection_injective I (by rw [hmul c, ← hcy])⟩

/-- **The rank-one dual basis of a principal ideal sheaf.** On an affine open where the ideal is
generated by a nonzerodivisor, the section of the ideal sheaf determined by that generator is a
basis of the ideal sheaf as a free module of rank one. -/
def dualBasisOneOfPrincipal (I : X.IdealSheafData) (U : X.affineOpens)
    {f : Γ(X, (U : X.Opens))} (hf : I.ideal U = Ideal.span {f})
    (hfnzd : f ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, (U : X.Opens))) :
    Stacks.SheafOfModules.DualBasisOne X.sheaf.obj
      (structureSheafRing X.toRingedSpace).property (idealSheafOfModules I) (U : X.Opens) :=
  have hfmem : ∃ y, idealSheafSection I y = f :=
    (mem_ideal_iff_exists_idealSheafSection I U f).1 (hf ▸ Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self f)
  Stacks.SheafOfModules.DualBasisOne.ofSmulBijective _ hfmem.choose
    (bijective_smulSectionMap_resSection I U hf hfnzd hfmem.choose_spec)

/-! ### The forward direction of Tag 01WS -/

/-- Off the support of the ideal sheaf there is an affine open on which the ideal is the unit
ideal: some section of the ideal does not vanish at the point, and on the basic open where it is
invertible it generates everything. -/
lemma exists_affineOpens_ideal_eq_top (I : X.IdealSheafData) {x : X} (hx : x ∉ I.support) :
    ∃ U : X.affineOpens, x ∈ (U : Set X) ∧ I.ideal U = ⊤ := by
  obtain ⟨U, hxU⟩ := exists_affineOpens_mem x
  rw [Scheme.IdealSheafData.mem_support_iff_of_mem hxU, Scheme.mem_zeroLocus_iff] at hx
  simp only [SetLike.mem_coe, not_forall, not_not] at hx
  obtain ⟨g, hgI, hxg⟩ := hx
  refine ⟨X.affineBasicOpen g, hxg, Ideal.eq_top_of_isUnit_mem _ ?_
    (X.toRingedSpace.isUnit_res_basicOpen g)⟩
  rw [← I.map_ideal_basicOpen U g]
  exact Ideal.mem_map_of_mem _ hgI

/-- **Stacks Project, Tag 01WS, the direction (2) ⇒ (1).** A closed subscheme which near every
point of its support is cut out, on an affine open, by a single nonzerodivisor is an effective
Cartier divisor.

The hypothesis is clause (2) of the tag: the points of `I.support` are the points of `D`, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.range_subschemeι`, and `I.ideal U = (f)` says that
`U ∩ D = Spec(Γ(X, U)/(f))`, by
`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.IdealSheafData.ker_subschemeι_app`.

Near such a point the generator gives a rank-one dual basis of the ideal sheaf
(`Stacks.Divisors.dualBasisOneOfPrincipal`), and off the support the ideal is the unit ideal,
generated by the nonzerodivisor `1`; the resulting dual bases cover `X`, so
`Stacks.Divisors.isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_forall_exists_dualBasisOne` applies.

The converse direction (1) ⇒ (2) is not proved: it needs that an invertible sheaf of modules is
locally free of rank one, which is the descent step
`StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.Invertible` records as missing. -/
@[stacks 01WS "(2) implies (1)", ega "IV 21.2.12" "partial"]
theorem isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_forall_mem_support (I : X.IdealSheafData)
    (h : ∀ x ∈ I.support, ∃ (U : X.affineOpens) (f : Γ(X, (U : X.Opens))),
      x ∈ (U : Set X) ∧ I.ideal U = Ideal.span {f} ∧
        f ∈ nonZeroDivisors Γ(X, (U : X.Opens))) :
    IsEffectiveCartierDivisor I := by
  refine isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_forall_exists_dualBasisOne I fun x => ?_
  by_cases hx : x ∈ I.support
  · obtain ⟨U, f, hxU, hf, hfnzd⟩ := h x hx
    exact ⟨(U : X.Opens), hxU, ⟨dualBasisOneOfPrincipal I U hf hfnzd⟩⟩
  · obtain ⟨U, hxU, hU⟩ := exists_affineOpens_ideal_eq_top I hx
    refine ⟨(U : X.Opens), hxU, ⟨dualBasisOneOfPrincipal I U
      (f := 1) (by rw [hU, Ideal.span_singleton_one]) (Submonoid.one_mem _)⟩⟩

/-- **The empty closed subscheme is an effective Cartier divisor.** It is cut out by the unit
ideal on every affine open, and the unit ideal is generated by the nonzerodivisor `1`. This is
the companion of `Stacks.Divisors.isLocallyPrincipal_top`, and it shows that the criterion above
is not vacuous. -/
theorem isEffectiveCartierDivisor_top :
    IsEffectiveCartierDivisor (⊤ : X.IdealSheafData) := by
  exact isEffectiveCartierDivisor_of_forall_mem_support _ fun _ hx => hx.elim

end Stacks.Divisors

end
